window.products.push({"id":1009371,"name":"Lehman's Cast Iron Skillet - Nitrogen Hardened Cookware, Tough but Lightweight, No Need to Season, Heatproof Glass Lid Included - 11 inch","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":42.98,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/516WB1wEb6L._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"This skillet is infused with nitrogen, creating a harder-than-common-cast-iron finish. It has all the benefits of cast iron but with a surface that can't be scratched off, will never chip and creates a non-stick surface It may just be the lightest iron skillet you'll find. Features a cool, smooth stainless steel handle. Comes with a heatproof glass lid so you can watch your food as it cooks - no splattering. Dimensions: Inside 11\"ID x 2\"D, Outside 11 1/8\"OD x 2 1/8\"H, Weight with lid 4 3/4 lb (just skillet 3 lb). Helpful Hint: Care and cleaning of cast iron cookware is easy! It may be just a little different from what you are used to, though. Unlike conventional seasoned cast iron cookware, this skillet can be scoured. Its non-stick properties are from nitrogen infused into the iron, not seasoning that only lies on the surface. So, scour to your heart's content! Hand washing is best. Washing in a dishwasher may cause stains. Stains can be removed by seasoning the pan. Seasoning: Seasoning is not needed, unlike other cast iron cookware. However, the non-stick properties of the pan can be slightly improved if you season it. Detailed instructions for this are included with the pan. You can season it by frying a batch of bacon or coating the pan with cooking oil and heating it in your oven. If you season it, keep in mind that scouring will remove the seasoning. To remove cooked-on food: Pour enough water into the skillet to cover the cooked-on residue. Bring the water to a rolling boil. Carefully pour off the water. Rinse the pan until cool. Wipe clean with a plastic scouring pad. If you seasoned the pan, this will not remove the seasoning. This process sterilizes the pan. You can dry and store the pan without washing it. Black residue left on the pan after cleaning? This is a harmless carbon residue left from cooking or seasoning. If it bothers you, you can remove it by gentle scouring","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/516WB1wEb6L._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Lehman's","source_asin":"B09Y65NC75","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-1009371","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09Y65NC75","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B09Y65NC75","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
